   "id": "events",
   "plain": "You can ask for a new decision with form SSA-44 if your income went down because of a life-changing event: marriage, divorce or a spouse's death; you or your spouse stopping or reducing work; losing income-producing property in a disaster; a pension plan ending or being cut; or an employer settlement after closure or bankruptcy.",
   "source": "https://www.ssa.gov/forms/ssa-44.html",
   "effective_from": null,
   "checked_on": "2026-11-23"
  },
  {
   "id": "proof",
   "plain": "Send proof of the event and of the lower income, such as a death certificate or a letter from your employer, and a signed copy of your tax return if you filed one.",
